youranmod.jei.locator_module.info=Locator Module (a location peripheral): goes into the locator module slot in the computer's interface.\nWhen a website asks for this computer's location, a system confirmation box pops up outside the screen, where web pages cannot click it. If you agree, the server signs a location proof for the computer's dimension and coordinates and hands it to the website, which checks it on the spot with the public key.\nWithout the module you can still go online; only websites that need a location will not work.
