youranmod.jei.arf_laser_cavity.info=Built with the Light Source blueprint at the Immersive Engineering Engineer's Workbench. It comes out empty.\nLiquid argon: IC2 Fluid Canning Machine or Immersive Engineering Bottling Machine, 10 mB at a time, up to 750 mB.\nFluorine and neon: IC2 Solid Canning Machine, one Alchemistry element at a time; each has a limit.\nThe mix of the three affects the strength of the laser; see "Expected output" in the tooltip.\nCraft it with an Immersive Engineering Floodlight into an Excimer Laser Light Source; crafting the light source alone takes it apart again, so it can be refilled and put back.
youranmod.jei.hene_laser_tube.info=Built with the Light Source blueprint (glass or quartz tube both work). It comes out empty.\nHelium and neon: IC2 Solid Canning Machine, one Alchemistry element at a time, up to 250 per tube. The mix affects the strength of the laser; see "Expected output" in the tooltip.\nPut it in the laser slot of the Alignment Table and add a Personal Computer Motherboard whose ROM is the laser alignment control program to use laser alignment.
youranmod.jei.excimer_light_source.info=Crafted from an ArF Laser Cavity and an Immersive Engineering Floodlight. Goes in the light source spot of the Lithography Machine, in place of the Mercury Light Source.\nResolution 0.05 μm. While exposing it draws about 20,000 FE per second (1024 FE/t), and every exposure uses up a little fluorine.
youranmod.jei.improved_resist.info=1000 mB of positive resist and 10 mB of IC2 UU-Matter make 1000 mB of improved positive resist.\nMachines: Immersive Engineering Refinery; or IC2 Canning Machine (enrich mode: positive resist in the input tank, a container of UU-Matter in the input slot; each run draws 10 mB from it).\nResolution 0.05 μm. Coating and development work as for positive resist.
